Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"ChargesEinsteinMaxwellScalarAsympt", "::", "usage"}], " ", "=",
   " ", "\"\<ChargesEinsteinMaxwellScalarAsympt[{xiU_,\[Lambda]_},{Ad_,\[Phi]_\
},{hdd_,ad_,var\[Phi]_},signatureg_,{index1_,index2_},{kin\[Phi]_,kinA_,\[Phi]\
Uneval_},{coordAsympt_,LimitAsympt_}, order_] compute asymptotically the \
surface charge in Einstein gravity coupled to Maxwell and one scalar field\n\
Need = metric and coord should be defined and RGtensors should have been \
executed prior to this procedure\nInput = A couple of (asymptotic) symmetry \
parameters : 'xiU' and '\[Lambda]' \n        The background gauge field 'Ad' \
and scalar fields '\[Phi]'\n        The variation of the metric 'hdd', gauge \
field 'ad' and scalar field 'var\[Phi]'\n\t    The signature of the metric \
'signatureg' (1 or -1)\n        A surface of codimension 2 specified by the \
two indices '{index1,index2}' in the coordinates coord that are fixed\n\t    \
The normalisation constants 'kinA[\[Phi]Uneval]', 'kin\[Phi][\[Phi]Uneval]' \
in the Lagrangian as a function of the special variable '\[Phi]Uneval'\n      \
  The coordinate to expand onto 'coordAsympt', the value of the coordinate at \
the limit 'LimitAsympt' and the number of terms wished in the final expansion \
'order' \nOutput = The components {index1,index2} of the surface charge \
associated with the symmetry (xiU,\[Lambda]) under the perturbation\nExtra \
output : ChargeSuppl : supplementary term with respect to the Iyer-Wald \
formula.\nConvention : The Lagrangian has the form\n        L = \
\!\(\*FractionBox[SqrtBox[\(signatureg\\\ g\)], \(16  \[Pi]\)]\)(R - \
\!\(\*FractionBox[\(1\), \(4\)]\)kinA[\[Phi]] \!\(\*SuperscriptBox[\(F\), \(\
\[Mu]\[Nu]\)]\)\!\(\*SubscriptBox[\(F\), \(\[Mu]\[Nu]\)]\) - \
\!\(\*FractionBox[\(1\), \(2\)]\)kin\[Phi][\[Phi]]\!\(\*SubscriptBox[\(\
\[PartialD]\), \(\[Mu]\)]\)\[Phi]\!\(\*SuperscriptBox[\(\[PartialD]\), \
\(\[Mu]\)]\)\[Phi])\n\>\""}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.449078349953125*^9, 3.44907845025*^9}, {
  3.449078599375*^9, 3.449078648984375*^9}, {3.449078723953125*^9,
